WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.626
Reinforcement learning now drives safety-critical
systems like autonomous vehicles,

00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:08.833
but adversarial perturbations to a policy's input
states can quietly steer it toward disaster.

00:00:08.913 --> 00:00:13.039
Many defenses improve robustness empirically,

00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:17.245
yet almost none can certify it with guarantees.

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:21.452
This paper introduces CROP,

00:00:21.532 --> 00:00:25.658
the first unified framework to certify robust
policies for reinforcement learning through functional smoothing.

00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:29.865
CROP certifies robustness at two levels: the
stability of the action taken at each state,

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:34.071
and a provable lower bound on the cumulative reward
across a whole trajectory.

00:00:34.151 --> 00:00:38.277
Using it,

00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:42.484
the authors benchmark nine existing robust RL
algorithms across four environments and

00:00:42.564 --> 00:00:46.690
show that their certificates are often tight.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.519
Reinforcement learning has moved into domains where
failure is costly,

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:54.042
such as autonomous driving and trading.

00:00:54.122 --> 00:00:59.801
But researchers have shown that an adversary who
slightly perturbs the state observations

00:00:59.881 --> 00:01:03.230
fed to an RL agent can reliably change its decisions.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:08.729
A wave of empirical defenses followed, only to be
defeated by newer adaptive attacks.

00:01:08.809 --> 00:01:13.970
What has been missing is certification: a way to
prove, rather than just observe,

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.534
that a trained policy stays reliable under every
perturbation within a bounded budget.

00:01:19.614 --> 00:01:23.610
This paper tackles exactly that gap for
reinforcement learning.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:27.835
The core motivation is trust.

00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:31.761
If you cannot prove a policy is robust,

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:35.686
then passing today's attacks tells you little about
tomorrow's.

00:01:35.766 --> 00:01:39.612
Randomized smoothing has become a leading tool for
certifying image classifiers,

00:01:39.692 --> 00:01:43.537
but reinforcement learning does not fit its mold.

00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:47.463
In classification the confidence output lives in a
known zero-to-one range and behaves like a probability;

00:01:47.543 --> 00:01:51.388
in Q-learning the value function has an unknown
range and its outputs are not probabilities at all.

00:01:51.468 --> 00:01:55.314
On top of that,

00:01:55.394 --> 00:01:59.239
a single action decision is not the whole story:
what ultimately matters is the reward

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:03.165
accumulated along an entire trajectory of decisions.

00:02:03.245 --> 00:02:07.090
CROP is designed to overcome both obstacles.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:11.322
CROP makes three main contributions.

00:02:11.402 --> 00:02:15.253
First,

00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:19.185
it defines two certification criteria for
reinforcement learning: robustness of the per-state action,

00:02:19.265 --> 00:02:23.117
and a lower bound on the cumulative reward.

00:02:23.197 --> 00:02:27.048
Second, it turns each criterion into an algorithm.

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:30.980
CROP-LoAct uses local randomized smoothing to
certify a radius around each state within

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.912
which the chosen action cannot change.

00:02:34.992 --> 00:02:38.843
CROP-GRe uses global smoothing to bound the
expected and percentile reward,

00:02:38.923 --> 00:02:42.775
and CROP-LoRe performs an adaptive tree search to
produce a much tighter absolute lower bound on reward.

00:02:42.855 --> 00:02:46.707
Third,

00:02:46.787 --> 00:02:50.638
the authors apply these tools to nine existing
robust RL algorithms across four environments,

00:02:50.718 --> 00:02:54.570
and release the results as an open leaderboard for
the community.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.573
The engine of CROP is functional smoothing.

00:02:57.653 --> 00:02:59.774
At each state, and for each action,

00:02:59.854 --> 00:03:05.306
the method adds Gaussian noise to the state and
averages the trained Q-network's output,

00:03:05.386 --> 00:03:07.570
producing a smoothed value function.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.656
A key lemma shows this smoothed function is
Lipschitz continuous,

00:03:11.736 --> 00:03:15.491
with a constant that shrinks as the smoothing
variance grows.

00:03:15.571 --> 00:03:16.812
From that continuity,

00:03:16.892 --> 00:03:22.596
Theorem 1 gives a certified radius: as long as the
perturbation is smaller than this radius,

00:03:22.676 --> 00:03:25.425
the smoothed policy's action does not change.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:30.706
The radius depends on the gap between the best and
runner-up smoothed action-values,

00:03:30.786 --> 00:03:32.089
revealing a trade-off,

00:03:32.169 --> 00:03:36.678
since more smoothing stabilizes the values but also
narrows their margin.

00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.062
For cumulative reward,

00:03:38.142 --> 00:03:44.537
global smoothing treats the whole trajectory as a
function to bound the expected and percentile reward,

00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:51.390
while the adaptive local search of CROP-LoRe grows
a trajectory tree to certify a tight absolute lower bound.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.748
To test the framework broadly,

00:03:55.828 --> 00:03:59.806
the authors run it on four environments spanning
very different regimes.

00:03:59.886 --> 00:04:03.864
Pong and Freeway are high-dimensional Atari games;

00:04:03.944 --> 00:04:07.922
CartPole is a classic low-dimensional control task;

00:04:08.002 --> 00:04:11.980
and Highway simulates autonomous driving.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.038
On these, they certify nine existing reinforcement
learning methods,

00:04:16.118 --> 00:04:20.096
ranging from standard training and Gaussian
augmentation to adversarial training,

00:04:20.176 --> 00:04:24.154
the SA-MDP variants, RadialRL, CARRL, NoisyNet, and
gradient-based DQN.

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:28.212
This makes CROP not just a single certificate but a
benchmark that places many robust RL methods on a common,

00:04:28.292 --> 00:04:32.270
provable footing.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.296
The certifications reveal clear and consistent winners.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:40.022
On Freeway,

00:04:40.102 --> 00:04:43.748
RadialRL achieves the highest certified radius
across every smoothing level,

00:04:43.828 --> 00:04:47.473
because it explicitly optimizes against worst-case
perturbations.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:51.199
On Pong, SA-MDP with the convex relaxation is the
most certifiably robust.

00:04:51.279 --> 00:04:54.925
Encouragingly,

00:04:55.005 --> 00:04:58.651
these certified rankings largely agree with what
people had observed empirically,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:02.377
which builds confidence in the certificates.

00:05:02.457 --> 00:05:06.103
The analysis also surfaces new structure: on Pong
every method shows a periodic pattern

00:05:06.183 --> 00:05:09.828
in its certified radius over time,

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:13.554
with robustness peaking at confident states such as
when the ball flies toward the paddle,

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:17.280
an insight that could guide future robust training.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.962
A central ablation studies the smoothing variance sigma.

00:05:22.042 --> 00:05:26.344
On Freeway,

00:05:26.424 --> 00:05:30.726
robustness for the strong methods keeps improving
as sigma grows all the way to one point zero,

00:05:30.806 --> 00:05:35.108
since Freeway tolerates large noise.

00:05:35.188 --> 00:05:39.490
On Pong the story differs: too much smoothing hurts,

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:43.872
and a moderate sigma between about zero point zero
one and zero point zero three works best for nearly all methods.

00:05:43.952 --> 00:05:48.254
The authors also compare their three reward bounds.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:52.636
The percentile bound is far tighter than the loose
expectation bound,

00:05:52.716 --> 00:05:57.018
and the absolute lower bound from CROP-LoRe often
matches the empirical reward under PGD attack exactly,

00:05:57.098 --> 00:06:01.400
a zero gap that demonstrates the certificates are
tight rather than merely valid.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.894
A few numbers capture the scope.

00:06:03.974 --> 00:06:09.172
CROP is the first unified certification framework
for reinforcement learning,

00:06:09.252 --> 00:06:13.627
working at both the action level and the
cumulative-reward level.

00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:19.454
It certifies nine existing robust RL methods across
four environments: Pong, Freeway,

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:20.962
CartPole, and Highway.

00:06:21.042 --> 00:06:24.869
It does so with three algorithms: CROP-LoAct for actions,

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:27.474
and CROP-GRe and CROP-LoRe for reward.

00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:32.272
The smoothing variance is pushed as high as one
point zero on Freeway,

00:06:32.352 --> 00:06:37.550
and reward robustness is reported through three
bounds, an expectation bound,

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.800
a fifty-percent percentile bound, and an absolute
lower bound.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:48.349
The lasting message of CROP is that robustness in
reinforcement learning need not be a matter of hope.

00:06:48.429 --> 00:06:50.310
By smoothing the value function,

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:54.905
you can prove that an agent's action stays fixed
within a certified radius,

00:06:54.985 --> 00:07:00.235
and you can prove a lower bound on the reward it
will collect under any bounded attack.

00:07:00.315 --> 00:07:03.238
Applied to nine methods across four environments,

00:07:03.318 --> 00:07:06.669
these certificates are not only correct but often tight,

00:07:06.749 --> 00:07:08.507
matching what attacks achieve.

00:07:08.587 --> 00:07:13.163
CROP turns robust RL into something you can measure
and compare on a common,

00:07:13.243 --> 00:07:14.450
provable leaderboard,

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:19.780
and invites the community to certify more methods
and more environments in future work.
